<title>ISRAEL: Israel Discount Bank Q2 net up.</title>
<headline>Israel Discount Bank Q2 net up.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Israel Discount Bank</p>
<p>			   (In thousands of shekels except EPS)</p>
<p>			 Q2 96     Q2 95	6-MTH 96    6-MTH 95</p>
<p>Income before	570,884   520,150    1,131,299   1,109,917</p>
<p>provision for</p>
<p>doubtful debt</p>
<p>Doubtful debt	110,995    67,399	188,528     130,507</p>
<p>provision</p>
<p>Operating, other    208,377  215,748	432,025     430,929</p>
<p>income</p>
<p>Net profit	     71,631   48,751	134,626     139,695</p>
<p>EPS			 0.77     0.52	   1.44	  1.50</p>
<p>Annualised yield on shareholders' equity for the second quarter of 1996 was 7.7 percent and for the first half of the year was 7.3 percent, similar to the yield for all of 1995, the bank said.</p>
<p>Consolidated assets of the bank as of June 30 were $23.2 billion, compared with $22.3 billion in the same period last year.</p>
<p>Shareholders equity on June 30 1996 totalled $1.20 billion.</p>
<p>Credit to the public on June 30 1996 totalled $12.7 billion, compared with $11.6 billion in the same period last year.</p>
<p>Deposits from the public totalled $19.4 billion, compared with $18.4 billion on June 30, 1995.</p>
<p>The board of directors declared an interim cash dividend of 35 million shekels.</p>
<p>- Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211</p>
</text>
